---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Bug1 = `let crew = ["Vega", "Orion", "Lyra", "Draco"];

function find(name)
{
  for (let i = 0; i < crew.length; i++)
  {
    if (crew[i] === name)
    {
      return i;
    }
    else
    {
      return -1;
    }
  }
}

console.log(find("Vega"));
console.log(find("Lyra"));
console.log(find("Nope"));`;

const Bug2 = `let ids = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50];
let target = 35;

let low = 0;
let high = ids.length - 1;

while (low <= high)
{
  let mid = Math.floor((low + high) / 2);

  if (ids[mid] === target)
  {
    console.log("found at " + mid);
    break;
  }

  if (ids[mid] < target)
  {
    low = mid;
  }
  else
  {
    high = mid - 1;
  }
}

console.log("done");`;

const Bug3 = `let ids = [40, 10, 50, 20, 30];

function binarySearch(list, target)
{
  let low = 0;
  let high = list.length - 1;

  while (low <= high)
  {
    let mid = Math.floor((low + high) / 2);

    if (list[mid] === target)
    {
      return mid;
    }

    if (list[mid] < target)
    {
      low = mid + 1;
    }
    else
    {
      high = mid - 1;
    }
  }

  return -1;
}

console.log("looking for 10 -> " + binarySearch(ids, 10));
console.log("looking for 50 -> " + binarySearch(ids, 50));
console.log("looking for 20 -> " + binarySearch(ids, 20));`;

const Bug4 = `let scores = [10, 20, 30];

function find(list, target)
{
  for (let i = 0; i < list.length; i++)
  {
    if (list[i] = target)
    {
      return i;
    }
  }
  return -1;
}

console.log("looking for 30 -> " + find(scores, 30));
console.log("the list is now " + scores);`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Debug Challenge: Search</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>
            Four searches. <b>Not one of them crashes.</b> There is no error
            message anywhere on this page, and that is the point of it.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Three of them give you a confident wrong answer. One never gives
            you an answer at all.</b>
          </p>

          <p>
            A search that returns <code>-1</code> looks exactly the same whether
            the item is genuinely missing or your code is broken. So you cannot
            debug these by reading the output. <b>You have to check the output
            against a list you can see.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="bugs">
          <h2>The Four Programs</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 1</h3>

          <p>
            This should find any name in the crew list. It finds exactly one of
            them.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug1} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 1" class="mb-3" />

          <p>
            <b>Also:</b> <code>"Lyra"</code> is in the list and the program says
            it is not. Say which line decided that, and on which pass of the
            loop.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 2</h3>

          <p>
            <b>This one does not stop.</b> 35 is not in the list, and the program
            never gets to the last line.
          </p>

          <p class="text-body-secondary">
            Read it before you run it. If you do run it, be ready to stop it.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug2} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 2" class="mb-3" />

          <p>
            <b>Also:</b> trace <code>low</code>, <code>mid</code>, and{" "}
            <code>high</code> until they stop changing, and write down the three
            values it gets stuck on. <b>One character fixes this.</b>
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 3</h3>

          <p>
            The procedure is a correct binary search. Copy it out and check it
            against Activity 2.10 if you like &mdash; there is nothing wrong with
            it.
          </p>

          <p>
            It reports that 10 and 20 are missing. Both are in the list. It finds
            50.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug3} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 3" class="mb-3" />

          <p>
            <b>Also:</b> the fix is not in the procedure. Say what it is, and then
            explain why 50 was found anyway.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 4</h3>

          <p>
            This should find 30 at index 2. It says index 0, and then the list
            has changed.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug4} frame="code" lang="javascript" title="Bug 4" class="mb-3" />

          <p>
            <b>Also:</b> this is one keystroke. Say what the condition on that
            line actually evaluates to, and why it counted as true.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            For each program: one sentence on what was wrong, the corrected line,
            and the answers to the <b>Also</b> questions.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>And one more, for the set as a whole:</b> three of these four gave
            a wrong answer with no error message. Name one thing you could add to
            a search program so that a wrong answer would be noticed.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>3 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1 class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash">
          Commence Debugging
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
